    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0705" n="685" xml:id="pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Executive Secretariat Files: NSC 81</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Executive Secretary of the National
                        Security Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        NSC 81</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-09-01">September 01, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Note by the Executive Secretary to the National
                        Security Council on United States Courses of Action With Respect to
                        Korea</hi>
                </p>
                <table>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#top">References: </cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">A. NSC
                            Action No. 338<anchor n="1" xml:id="d486-f1"/>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">B. Memos for NSC from Executive Secretary, subject: “Future United
                            States Policy with Respect to Korea”, dated July 17<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d486-f2"/> and August 30, 1950<anchor n="3" xml:id="d486-f3"
                            />
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>Pursuant to the President’s request the enclosed report on the subject, prepared
                    by the NSC Staff, is submitted herewith for
                    consideration by the National Security Council and the Secretary of the Treasury
                    at the next regularly scheduled Council meeting on Thursday, September 7,
                    1950.</p>
                <p>It is recommended that, if this report is adopted, it be submitted to the
                    President for consideration with the recommendation that he approve the
                    Conclusions contained therein and direct their implementation by all executive
                    departments and agencies of the U.S. Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay,
                            Jr</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d486-a1.xml" xpointer="d486-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d486-f1" n="1" xml:id="d486-f1-content">
                <p>Taken at the 64th meeting of the National Security Council on August 10, it
                    expressed agreement that the NSC Staff should
                    expedite work on the preparation of the requested report on Future U.S. Policy
                    With Respect to North Korea.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d486-f2" n="2" xml:id="d486-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg410">p. 410</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d486-f3" n="3" xml:id="d486-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed; it forwarded a memorandum dated August 29 from the Office of the
                    Secretary of Defense, in which the President concurred, requesting the NSC Staff to expedite work on its report so that it
                    could be considered at the NSC meeting on
                    September 7, 1950. (NSC files)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
